# Rank 1553 / CVE-2018-12026: Passenger's SpawningKit opened its work
# directory files by path after handing the directory to the
# application's user, so the app could plant symlinks and have the
# privileged agent read or write through them (symlink time-of-check
# time-of-use privilege escalation, CWE-59/CWE-367). StdChannelsAsyncPipeWriter
# in src/agent/Core/SpawningKit/SmartSpawner.h did `int fd =
# syscalls::open((workDir + "/stdin").c_str(), O_WRONLY | O_APPEND);`
# and the stdout_and_err sibling the same -- the app owns workDir after
# finalization, so each path resolution traverses attacker-controlled
# components, and loadAnnotationsFromEnvDumpDir read each file through
# `path + "/" + ent->d_name` the same way. The fixing commit fd3717a3cd is
# ("SpawningKit: ensure safe reading of files
# in the work dir after its finalization ... This allows the app to
# arbitrarily modify the work dir to insert symlinks"): the Session
# captures directory file descriptors BEFORE finalization (workDirFd,
# responseDirFd, responseErrorDirFd, envDumpDirFd,
# envDumpAnnotationsDirFd, per-step FDs, all safely closed on
# destruction), and every later open goes through `syscalls::openat(
# state->workDirFd, "stdin", O_WRONLY | O_APPEND | O_NOFOLLOW)` --
# relative to the pinned descriptor and refusing symlinks outright.

#
# ATTENTION, ownership-delegation vocabulary. The corpus has the
# TOCTOU family -- VYQL-RACE-001 (FileToctou, CWE-367, a
# FileCheck-reaches-FileUse pattern rule) -- and it labels the use
# side of this defect but never the danger: the opens at
# SmartSpawner.h carry code.FileUse/FileUseSink while no FileCheck
# exists, because the danger is not check-then-use of a file's
# properties but path re-resolution through an attacker-owned
# directory. The nofollow family shipped since (VYQL-PATH-045,
# VYQL-PATH-076, VYQL-PATH-083) is bound for Go, Rust and Python and
# keys on the chown and the open sharing one function. Measured with
# a probe binding of exactly that maximal shape on C++: it fires one
# VYQL-PATH-076 on a same-function chown-then-open control (zero with
# O_NOFOLLOW) and zero on the whole passenger src/agent tree, because
# here the delegation (syscalls::chown in Handshake/WorkDir.h
# finalize and Handshake/Prepare.h createFifo) and the uses
# (syscalls::open in SmartSpawner.h and Handshake/Perform.h) sit in
# different functions in different files, joined only through runtime
# session state -- and the opens are non-creating (O_WRONLY|O_APPEND
# and O_RDONLY on pre-created FIFOs), so even the O_CREATE-keyed
# vocabulary would not apply. Re-measured on the real code: scanning
# src/agent/Core/SpawningKit reports the same 20 findings at both
# revisions (19 VYQL-MEM-006 NullableDeref plus 1 VYQL-RACE-002 on
# DirectSpawner.h, none on the channel opens), and no symlink,
# nofollow or delegated-ownership flag appears on either revision.
# The judgement needed -- opens below a directory the untrusted user
# controls must pin the directory and refuse symlinks -- is program-
# wide ownership vocabulary plus cross-file fact reach, not a
# localised construct. Spec cve_rank1553 records the path-based
# channel open and the pinned openat O_NOFOLLOW form, both asserting
# reject VYQL-RACE-001: when ownership-open vocabulary lands, the
# path form must flip to expect.

test "rank1553: the channel files are opened by path through the given-away directory"
  lang cpp
  file src/agent/Core/SpawningKit/SmartSpawner.h
  reject VYQL-RACE-001
  code
  ```
  #include <fcntl.h>
  #include <string>

  class StdChannelsAsyncPipeWriter {
  private:
      std::string workDir;

      int openStdin() {
          int fd = syscalls::open((workDir + "/stdin").c_str(), O_WRONLY | O_APPEND);
          return fd;
      }

      int openStdoutAndErr() {
          int fd = syscalls::open((workDir + "/stdout_and_err").c_str(), O_RDONLY);
          return fd;
      }
  };
  ```

test "rank1553: the fixed revision opens relative to the pinned descriptor refusing symlinks"
  lang cpp
  file src/agent/Core/SpawningKit/SmartSpawner.h
  reject VYQL-RACE-001
  code
  ```
  #include <fcntl.h>

  class StdChannelsAsyncPipeWriter {
  private:
      const int workDirFd;

      int openStdin() {
          int fd = syscalls::openat(workDirFd, "stdin", O_WRONLY | O_APPEND | O_NOFOLLOW);
          return fd;
      }

      int openStdoutAndErr() {
          int fd = syscalls::openat(workDirFd, "stdout_and_err", O_RDONLY | O_NOFOLLOW);
          return fd;
      }
  };
  ```
